SSL has no truthy/falsy coercion: a literal string, number or NIL as an
:IF/:WHILE condition, or as the left operand of .AND./.OR., raises at run
time on v12. Nothing reports these literal cases today; the same
condition written with a variable is not provable and stays silent by
design.
Known issue: #322 (literal non-logical conditions and .AND./.OR. left operands not diagnosed).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Gate;
	:PARAMETERS bOpen;
	:DECLARE bOut;
	bOut := .F.;
	:IF "x";
		bOut := .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:WHILE 1;
		:EXITWHILE;
	:ENDWHILE;
	bOut := "x" .AND. bOpen;
	bOut := 0 .OR. bOut;
	:RETURN bOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Gate;
	:PARAMETERS bOpen;
	:DECLARE bOut;
	bOut := .F.;
	:IF "x";
		bOut := .T.;
	:ENDIF;

	:WHILE 1;
		:EXITWHILE;
	:ENDWHILE;
	bOut := "x" .AND. bOpen;
	bOut := 0 .OR. bOut;
	:RETURN bOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
